From 7bb713b72a9e7c26a3520c9b923ab61d4754fe2e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joerg Roedel <joerg.roedel@amd.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 17:08:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 08/20] accel/kvm: Route device interrupts by plane

Carry the originating device's plane through emulated PCI MSI memory
transactions and select the matching plane for KVM_SIGNAL_MSI.

Pass the source device through IRQFD registration as well. This makes
assigned-device MSI and MSI-X use the device plane while retaining the
machine default for synthetic and legacy callers. Deassignment uses the
same plane as assignment because the plane property becomes immutable at
realization.
